{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4iyJ6pYZK1bLgBkLKxw7z","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tImplement leave-service API\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone3 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t2\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** leave-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/leave-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Handle CRUD operations for leave requests\n- Track and update leave balances when requests are approved\n- Validate leave request date ranges\n- Filter leave requests by employee userId\n- Filter pending leave requests by managerId (for manager's direct reports)\n- Integrate with user-service to retrieve manager's direct reports\n- Enforce business rules (sufficient balance, valid status transitions)\n- Provide health check endpoint\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Must call user-service to resolve manager-to-reports relationships\n- Leave balance calculation must account for date range (inclusive)\n- Status transitions should only allow pending -> approved/rejected\n- Insufficient balance should block approval with 400 error\n- In-memory storage is acceptable for this implementation\n- Service must listen on port 9090\n- All responses should be JSON formatted\n\n## Component Dependencies\nThis component depends on the following components. You MUST:\n1. Declare each as a dependency in `workload.yaml` — OpenChoreo injects the resolved URL as an environment variable at runtime.\n2. Use the injected environment variable in your application code — **never hardcode service URLs**.\n\n- **user-service** → use env var `USER_SERVICE_URL`\n\nAdd this to your `workload.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\ndependencies:\n  endpoints:\n    - component: user-service\n      name: http\n      visibility: project\n      envBindings:\n        address: USER_SERVICE_URL\n```\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root of your component directory to declare endpoints and dependencies. Refer to the OpenChoreo workload configuration guidance in your skill for the correct format, endpoint types, dependency wiring, and the SPA nginx proxy pattern for frontend components.\n\nThe platform will handle git commit, push, build, and deploy automatically.\n## OpenAPI Spec\n\n```yaml\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Leave Service API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Manages leave requests, approvals, and balance tracking\npaths:\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health check\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Service is healthy\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    example: ok\n  /leave-requests:\n    post:\n      summary: Submit a new leave request\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequestInput'\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: Leave request created\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid input\n    get:\n      summary: List leave requests\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n          description: Filter by employee userId\n        - name: managerId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n          description: Filter by manager userId to see pending requests for their reports\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave requests\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n  /leave-requests/{requestId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get a single leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave request details\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n    patch:\n      summary: Update leave request status (approve/reject)\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequestUpdate'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request updated\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid status transition\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n  /leave-balance/{userId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave balance for a user\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave balance\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveBalance'\n        '404':\n          description: User not found\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    LeaveRequestInput:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - userId\n        - startDate\n        - endDate\n      properties:\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n    LeaveRequest:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n        updatedAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n    LeaveRequestUpdate:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - status\n      properties:\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [approved, rejected]\n    LeaveBalance:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        totalDays:\n          type: integer\n        usedDays:\n          type: integer\n        remainingDays:\n          type: integer\n```\n\n## Agent Instructions\nImplement a Go service using net/http listening on port 9090. Store leave requests and balances in memory. Each leave request has id (UUID), userId, startDate, endDate, status (pending/approved/rejected), createdAt, updatedAt. Initialize each user with 20 total leave days. POST /leave-requests accepts userId, startDate, endDate, creates a new request with status=pending, returns 201 with the created object. Validate that endDate >= startDate, return 400 otherwise. GET /leave-requests with query param userId returns all requests for that user. GET /leave-requests with query param managerId calls user-service at http://user-service:9090/users/{managerId}/reports to get direct report IDs, then returns all pending requests for those users. PATCH /leave-requests/{requestId} accepts status (approved or rejected). When approved, calculate days between startDate and endDate (inclusive), subtract from user's totalDays, update usedDays. Return 400 if insufficient balance. GET /leave-balance/{userId} returns totalDays, usedDays, remainingDays. GET /health returns {\"status\":\"ok\"}. Log all requests. Handle 404 for missing resources.\n\n## General Constraints\n- Write ALL files in the current working directory (do NOT create files outside it).\n- The component must have a Dockerfile for containerized builds.\n- Implement the full API contract from the task — every endpoint must be functional.\n- Use the dependencies listed to understand what other services this component talks to.\n- The app MUST start without any required environment variables — use sensible hardcoded defaults for all config (JWT secrets, DB paths, API URLs, etc.). Environment variables may override defaults but must never be required.\n- Do NOT stub or mock — write real, working implementations.\n- Do NOT run, start, or execute the application server locally. Only write source files. The platform builds and deploys your code automatically — local execution is unnecessary and will cause port conflicts.\n- If you must run a quick compile check (e.g. `go build`, `tsc --noEmit`), do so without starting a server. Never use `go run`, `npm start`, `node server.js`, or any command that starts a long-running process.\n\n## Working Directory\nAll file operations must happen inside this directory:\n\n```\n/Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/leave-service\n```\n\nBefore you do anything else, navigate there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/leave-service\n```\n\nDo NOT create files outside this directory. Do NOT `cd` elsewhere during your work.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d8d9b8d-a266-4879-bdba-7bc971617fd9","uuid":"ee5d01f3-f031-4b5d-86f8-9e76d4919cfc","timestamp":"2026-05-02T20:00:19.443Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tImplement leave-service API\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone3 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t2\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** leave-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/leave-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Handle CRUD operations for leave requests\n- Track and update leave balances when requests are approved\n- Validate leave request date ranges\n- Filter leave requests by employee userId\n- Filter pending leave requests by managerId (for manager's direct reports)\n- Integrate with user-service to retrieve manager's direct reports\n- Enforce business rules (sufficient balance, valid status transitions)\n- Provide health check endpoint\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Must call user-service to resolve manager-to-reports relationships\n- Leave balance calculation must account for date range (inclusive)\n- Status transitions should only allow pending -> approved/rejected\n- Insufficient balance should block approval with 400 error\n- In-memory storage is acceptable for this implementation\n- Service must listen on port 9090\n- All responses should be JSON formatted\n\n## Component Dependencies\nThis component depends on the following components. You MUST:\n1. Declare each as a dependency in `workload.yaml` — OpenChoreo injects the resolved URL as an environment variable at runtime.\n2. Use the injected environment variable in your application code — **never hardcode service URLs**.\n\n- **user-service** → use env var `USER_SERVICE_URL`\n\nAdd this to your `workload.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\ndependencies:\n  endpoints:\n    - component: user-service\n      name: http\n      visibility: project\n      envBindings:\n        address: USER_SERVICE_URL\n```\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root of your component directory to declare endpoints and dependencies. Refer to the OpenChoreo workload configuration guidance in your skill for the correct format, endpoint types, dependency wiring, and the SPA nginx proxy pattern for frontend components.\n\nThe platform will handle git commit, push, build, and deploy automatically.\n## OpenAPI Spec\n\n```yaml\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Leave Service API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Manages leave requests, approvals, and balance tracking\npaths:\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health check\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Service is healthy\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    example: ok\n  /leave-requests:\n    post:\n      summary: Submit a new leave request\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequestInput'\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: Leave request created\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid input\n    get:\n      summary: List leave requests\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n          description: Filter by employee userId\n        - name: managerId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n          description: Filter by manager userId to see pending requests for their reports\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave requests\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n  /leave-requests/{requestId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get a single leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave request details\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n    patch:\n      summary: Update leave request status (approve/reject)\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequestUpdate'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request updated\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid status transition\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n  /leave-balance/{userId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave balance for a user\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave balance\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveBalance'\n        '404':\n          description: User not found\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    LeaveRequestInput:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - userId\n        - startDate\n        - endDate\n      properties:\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n    LeaveRequest:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n        updatedAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n    LeaveRequestUpdate:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - status\n      properties:\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [approved, rejected]\n    LeaveBalance:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        userId:\n          type: string\n        totalDays:\n          type: integer\n        usedDays:\n          type: integer\n        remainingDays:\n          type: integer\n```\n\n## Agent Instructions\nImplement a Go service using net/http listening on port 9090. Store leave requests and balances in memory. Each leave request has id (UUID), userId, startDate, endDate, status (pending/approved/rejected), createdAt, updatedAt. Initialize each user with 20 total leave days. POST /leave-requests accepts userId, startDate, endDate, creates a new request with status=pending, returns 201 with the created object. Validate that endDate >= startDate, return 400 otherwise. GET /leave-requests with query param userId returns all requests for that user. GET /leave-requests with query param managerId calls user-service at http://user-service:9090/users/{managerId}/reports to get direct report IDs, then returns all pending requests for those users. PATCH /leave-requests/{requestId} accepts status (approved or rejected). When approved, calculate days between startDate and endDate (inclusive), subtract from user's totalDays, update usedDays. Return 400 if insufficient balance. GET /leave-balance/{userId} returns totalDays, usedDays, remainingDays. GET /health returns {\"status\":\"ok\"}. Log all requests. Handle 404 for missing resources.\n\n## General Constraints\n- Write ALL files in the current working directory (do NOT create files outside it).\n- The component must have a Dockerfile for containerized builds.\n- Implement the full API contract from the task — every endpoint must be functional.\n- Use the dependencies listed to understand what other services this component talks to.\n- The app MUST start without any required environment variables — use sensible hardcoded defaults for all config (JWT secrets, DB paths, API URLs, etc.). Environment variables may override defaults but must never be required.\n- Do NOT stub or mock — write real, working implementations.\n- Do NOT run, start, or execute the application server locally. Only write source files. The platform builds and deploys your code automatically — local execution is unnecessary and will cause port conflicts.\n- If you must run a quick compile check (e.g. `go build`, `tsc --noEmit`), do so without starting a server. Never use `go run`, `npm start`, `node server.js`, or any command that starts a long-running process.\n\n## Working Directory\nAll file operations must happen inside this directory:\n\n```\n/Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/leave-service\n```\n\nBefore you do anything else, navigate there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/leave-service\n```\n\nDo NOT create files outside this directory. Do NOT `cd` elsewhere during your work.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
